<title>USA: EU meat negotiator to stay in U.S. over weekend.</title>
<headline>EU meat negotiator to stay in U.S. over weekend.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lars Hoelgaard, the lead European Union negotiator in meat trade talks with the United States, will stay in Washington during the weekend, an EU spokeswoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>However, the spokeswoman said it appeared unlikely there would be discussions during the weekend.</p>
<p>Hundreds of millions of dollars of trade in meat, poultry, dairy and pet food were at stake in the so-called veterinary equivalency talks. An agreement would allow each side to accept meat shipments even if different means were used to assure food safety.</p>
<p>Without an agreement, the trans-Atlantic trade could be disrupted beginning April 1.</p>
</text>
